+# Off-map handover smoke — interrupted tail
+
+Build SHA-256: `3173d8f1d54b32ec3468729967f0c7315c265092e071f018b2aaee178d13e49b`.
+
+The short browser run passed all 20 recorded assertions through station-only farm bounds, separate owner scene, real entry/start, 44px Fold controls, scheduled lightning, dark spectral-pursuit encounter, gentle-mode lightning suppression, Exit, and a byte-identical farm save/paid ledger. Both screenshots show the exact build.
+
+The run then timed out waiting for a refusal notice after requesting fullscreen under Chromium's managed `FullscreenAllowed: false` policy. `checks.json` correctly remains `passed: false`; this is **not** a completed all-pass report. No page/console error or external runtime request was observed. The native fullscreen policy tail is now excluded explicitly in the reusable harness; successful OS fullscreen still needs a normal browser.
+
+Full final-build economic/save-load replay, all five final visual encounters, portrait/landscape phone layouts, physical Fold performance and native fullscreen remain lead verification work. Earlier functional and mobile results are historical and are not relabelled as this final build.
