+# Integrated core and POV verification
+
+**107/107 browser checks pass** against the immutable HTML SHA-256 `c429348aeb0ed45e53dbd3fd75a383636fa28b38fd3b82777dd65bcc1ea57653`.
+
+The single sequential browser run covers purchase gates and prices, a genuine queue and paid off-map departure, exact once-only ticket accounting, same guest purses, physical station picking, owner input ownership, pause/visibility/replay/Exit, all five cue IDs, unchanged farm saves and paid ledgers, real save/reload, background unloading, six/eight-seat tiers, scare purchases/toggles and footfall. Management and paused-ride layouts fit phone portrait, phone landscape and unfolded Fold viewports with 44px controls and no horizontal overflow.
+
+Resource verification renders every lurking/reveal interval, then repeats a complete warmed cycle: **60 geometries/16 textures → 60 geometries/16 textures**. The earlier strict first-upload failure is retained in the separate historical `release/` report; it is not hidden or relabelled.
+
+The normal-motion visual pass captures the station, rear boarding and all five scenes. A scheduled single lightning flash is checked through the owner status. The forest and scares occupy a separate off-map scene; the farm shows the station. Screenshots were visually inspected: the close scarecrow, ceiling spider, wet-haired girl, raised wraith and prison-bus ghoul are present in a dark, enclosed forest. Wagon posts naturally obscure portions of some actors at particular moments; the bus framing can receive later polish.
+
+No page/console errors, no external runtime asset requests and one main WebGL canvas. This is SwiftShader with the performance profile, bloom/shadows/mist/lake lights disabled, and muted audio. Audio composition/lifecycle has separate Node coverage; this run does not claim listening review or physical Z Fold frame-rate measurements. Chromium's managed `FullscreenAllowed:false` policy prevents a successful native fullscreen check. The fullscreen button remains available and the returned farm remains usable.
+
+Any later station-only tile/edge-clipping refinement has a separate build hash and report. Its results should supplement this full core/POV run rather than replacing this pinned artifact hash.
